<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul stock dealers call for steps to boost bourse.</title>
<headline>Seoul stock dealers call for steps to boost bourse.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Securities Dealers' Association on Thursday called for steps to boost the Seoul stock market, including the expansion of the foreign share ownership ceiling to 30 percent this year from the current 20 percent.</p>
<p>The call was made when Lee Hoi-chang, chairman of the ruling New Korea Party, met association chairman Youn Young-kyu, an association official said.</p>
